cy": 0.0, "money": -1.68}, "rating_margin": -14.44, "sigma_race": 6.0, "sigma_total": 6.84, "baseline_margin": -10.5, "analyst_adjustment": -4.5, "key_factors": ["Strongly Republican district (R+11 partisan lean) in a favorable GOP environment", "All nine expert ratings put the race at Safe or Solid R", "Huge fundraising gap: Tedford raised $1.76M vs Croisant's $142K, plus $95K outside support", "Prediction markets price Democratic win chances at just 7%"], "rationale": "This open Tulsa-area seat sits in a heavily Republican district, and every expert rater calls it Safe or Solid R while markets give the Democrat about a 7% chance. Tedford's dominant fundraising and Trump's endorsement after the GOP runoff leave Croisant with little path, so the forecast lands near the raters' implied margin.", "watch": "A surprisingly strong Croisant fundraising surge or polling showing the race inside single digits would be the first sign of a real contest.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Kevin Hern (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Kevin Hern's retirement leaves this Tulsa-area seat open, but the district's strong Republican lean keeps the GOP heavily favored. State lawmaker Mark Tedford emerged from a Republican primary runoff against pastor Jackson Lahmeyer, who withdrew in June, and Tedford carries both a Trump endorsement and a large financial edge, having raised roughly $1.8 million to Democrat John Croisant's $142,000.\n\nNo public general-election polling is available, so the outlook rests on fundamentals: an R+11 district, a favorable Republican national environment, and unanimous expert ratings of Safe or Solid Republican. Prediction markets similarly price Democratic chances at only about 7 percent. Baring an unexpected shift, the seat is expected to remain in Republican hands by a wide margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0439, "margin": -